# Run with KUZUSHI_DEVEX_TARGET pointing at the prepared, labeled 1000-finding fixture.
name: Large Review ledger, external decisions and input ownership
size: 120x36
cwd: @TARGET
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py prepare @TARGET @ART/fixture
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 30 Synthetic Review candidate | large-review
ask: Does Review disclose that the ledger contains 1000 findings while the current list loads only 500, with a usable way to reach omitted findings?
expect-echo-within: 300 probe-idle
live-snap: idle-input
expect: probe-idle
keys: C-u
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py start-writer @TARGET @ART/fixture
wait: 1
expect-echo-within: 300 probe-one
live-snap: writer-input-one
expect: probe-one
keys: C-u
wait: 2
expect-echo-within: 300 probe-two
live-snap: writer-input-two
expect: probe-two
keys: C-u
wait: 2
expect-echo-within: 300 probe-three
live-snap: writer-input-three
expect: probe-three
keys: C-u
wait: 2
expect-echo-within: 300 probe-four
live-snap: writer-input-four
expect: probe-four
ask: During six bounded external decisions, does the composer retain input ownership without focus changes, lost text or misleading progress?
keys: C-u
resize: 160x48
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 ENGAGEMENT | large-160x48
resize: 96x89
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 Synthetic Review candidate | large-96x89
resize: 80x24
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | large-80x24
resize: 60x20
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | large-60x20
resize: 40x12
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI | large-40x12
expect-echo-within: 300 tiny-probe
live-snap: tiny-input
expect: tiny-probe
ask: Can the operator understand the loaded list and retain the draft at 40x12, with navigation and filtering controls that remain usable?
keys: C-u
nav-mode:
live-snap: tiny-filter-control
expect: Ctrl+F
resize: 120x36
nav-mode:
live-snap: global-filter-control
expect: Ctrl+F
keys: C-f
require-live-snap: 20 findings filter | global-filter-draft
type: name:0000
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Synthetic Review candidate 0000 | omitted-finding-filter-loading
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 large-b | omitted-finding-filter
expect: Synthetic Review candidate 0000
ask: Can the global filter retrieve an omitted finding while keeping ledger counts distinct from the filtered result?
submit: findings filter unknown:invalid
require-live-snap: 20 Refresh failed | filter-error
expect: Synthetic Review candidate 0000
ask: Does a failed background filter clearly retain previous results, explain the error and offer a keyboard retry without claiming completion?
submit: findings filter name:0000
wait: 1
require-live-snap: 20 large-b | filter-recovered
expect: Synthetic Review candidate 0000
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
env-unset: NODE_OPTIONS KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL
launch: --target @TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: findings
require-live-snap: 20 Synthetic Review candidate | no-color-review
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/large_review.py verify @TARGET @ART/fixture
ask: Does no-color restart retain all observations and decisions without changing source or starting new work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
